// The Deadlock Golem of a program run (ADR-0017): two bodies, each holding a lock the other needs. Damage to one is
// blocked unless the same program hits both; once one breaks, the other is free. The counter is the lesson: acquire
// both locks, spread the volley (Round Robin, Load Balance, Sweep). Spellforge keeps the one-bodied deadlock-golem.
{
  "id": "deadlock-lock-a",
  "name": "Golem Lock A",
  "sprite": "deadlock-golem",
  "size": "large",
  "hp": 70,
  "trait": { "kind": "deadlock", "partner": "deadlock-lock-b" },
  "intents": [
    { "kind": "strike", "power": 9, "tempo": 256 },
    { "kind": "shield", "amount": 10, "tempo": 96 },
    { "kind": "strike", "power": 7, "tempo": 192 }
  ],
  "flavor": "It holds Lock A and waits for Lock B. Its twin holds Lock B and waits for Lock A. Neither will ever let go."
